/**
 * @file
 * @page DonnerSvgTool donner-cli CLI Tool
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolOverview Overview
 *
 * `donner-cli` is a command line utility for rendering SVG files to PNG and previewing output in
 * terminal environments. A convenience wrapper is checked in at `tools/donner-cli`, which is the
 * recommended way to invoke it from inside the repository.
 *
 * Build and run:
 * ```sh
 * tools/donner-cli input.svg
 * ```
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolBackend Rendering backend
 *
 * Published native packages contain `donner-cli`, its executable-adjacent `donner-assets`
 * directory, and licenses. Keep these files together when relocating an installation; rendering
 * works offline and reports an error if a required resource is missing or corrupt.
 *
 * `donner-cli` always renders with Donner's CPU (tiny-skia) backend, under
 * every build configuration. A one-shot command-line render cannot amortize
 * the GPU backend's fixed device and shader setup cost, so the CPU path is
 * faster for single-frame output. The GPU (Geode) backend is Donner's
 * interactive renderer, used by long-lived surfaces such as the editor,
 * where that setup cost is paid once across many frames.
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolFlags Common flags
 *
 * - `--output <png>`: Output filename (default `output.png`).
 * - `--width <px>` / `--height <px>`: Override render size.
 * - `--scale <factor>`: Scale the document's intrinsic size, for example `--scale 2` for a 2x
 *   render. Cannot be combined with `--width` or `--height`, and each scaled side must be at most
 *   65535 pixels.
 * - `--preview`: Show a terminal preview.
 * - `--interactive`: Enable mouse-driven terminal selection mode (implies `--preview`).
 * - `--quiet`: Suppress parser warnings.
 * - `--verbose`: Enable verbose renderer logs.
 * - `--experimental`: Enable experimental parser features.
 * - `--help`: Print usage.
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolGif Animated GIF export
 *
 * `--gif <file.gif>` renders a declarative (SMIL) animation to a looping animated GIF instead of
 * a PNG. Frames sample document time `start + i / fps` for every frame index `i` that falls before
 * `--end`. When `(end - start) * fps` is a whole number, the animation loops seamlessly from `end`
 * back to `start`; otherwise the last frame is shown for a full frame period. The canvas keeps its
 * size at `--start` for every frame, and each side is limited to 65535 pixels. An export is limited
 * to 10000 frames and 2^28 rendered pixels in total. The encoded file, encoder workspace, and
 * renderer surfaces each have separate 256 MiB limits; the command also admits its snapshot and
 * fitted-frame buffers within the workspace limit before entering the frame loop.
 *
 * - `--end <s>`: Animation end time in seconds (required).
 * - `--start <s>`: First frame's document time in seconds (default 0).
 * - `--fps <n>`: Frames per second (default 20, at least about 0.0016, the slowest rate a GIF frame
 *   delay can represent). GIF delays are whole centiseconds, so the delays alternate as needed to
 *   keep the total duration exact.
 * - `--scale`, `--width` and `--height` set the GIF size as they do for PNG output.
 * - `--background <color>`: Composite onto an opaque CSS color and produce an opaque GIF. Without
 *   it, the GIF keeps binary transparency: pixels below 50% opacity become transparent. Transparent
 *   exports reserve color-table index 0 consistently so common decoders clear disposed frames and
 *   loop restarts to transparency.
 *
 * Each frame gets its own color table. Frames with at most 256 colors (255 without
 * `--background`, which reserves one entry for transparency) are stored exactly; busier
 * frames are reduced with median cut, which keeps large flat colors exact. Identical consecutive
 * frames are merged into one longer frame, and opaque GIFs store only the changed region of each
 * frame.
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolExamples Examples
 *
 * ```sh
 * # Render to PNG
 * tools/donner-cli input.svg --output output.png
 *
 * # Terminal preview mode
 * tools/donner-cli input.svg --preview
 *
 * # Interactive mode
 * tools/donner-cli input.svg --interactive
 *
 * # Animated GIF of the first 4 seconds at 20 fps and twice the intrinsic size
 * tools/donner-cli input.svg --gif output.gif --end 4 --fps 20 --scale 2 --background white
 * ```
 *
 * @note `tools/donner-cli` is a thin shell wrapper that invokes
 *       `bazel run //donner/svg/tool:donner-cli -- <args>` with Bazel's progress/info output
 *       suppressed so the tool behaves like a normal CLI. The underlying Bazel target can also
 *       be invoked directly.
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolPreview Terminal preview
 *
 * `--preview` renders the SVG directly in the terminal using Unicode quadrant block characters
 * with 24-bit truecolor foreground and background, giving 2x2 sub-pixels per character cell.
 *
 * @image html donner_svg_preview_icon.svg width=640
 *
 * @section DonnerSvgToolInteractive Interactive mode
 *
 * `--interactive` implies `--preview` and adds mouse-driven selection: hover over the terminal
 * image to see the element under the cursor, and click to lock the selection.
 * The right-hand pane shows the DOM path and computed style of the selected element.
 */
